# Story 73: What Are Autonomous Agents? (50s)
# Hook: Headless AI workers. No terminal, no pane -- just a brain with tools.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-073-what-are-autonomous-agents.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Headless AI workers. No terminal, no pane -- just a brain with tools.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh. Every pane is a shell plus an agent -- but autonomous agents live entirely in the background.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
Double-press Escape twice to reach rysh mode, where the double-hash system commands live.

[00:14.0 --> 00:24.0]
Spawn an agent with a name and a system prompt. It has no PTY and no terminal -- just its own AgenticActor running independently in the workspace.

[00:24.0 --> 00:32.0]
Check ##agent list to see every agent and its status. Created via ##agent spawn, prompted with @name, controlled with @@name.

[00:32.0 --> 00:44.0]
Talk to it with the at-sign prefix from any input mode. The agent runs the prompt with full tool access in the background.

[00:44.0 --> 00:50.0]
Autonomous agents: tireless workers you spawn, prompt, and command -- without ever opening a pane.

